description:
### System Info

Transformers: 5.23.0.dev0
Commit: acf8004ec93d3d3195ea4945c693ff1c8959374e
PyTorch: 2.11.0+cu130
Platform: Linux
GPU: NVIDIA Tesla T4
Model: HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM-256M-Instruct
Affected: ImageTextToTextPipeline, AnyToAnyPipeline


<html>
<body>
<!--StartFragment--><h3><span>Description</span></h3><p><span>Multimodal pipelines crash during full-text response reconstruction when the final assistant prefill has string-valued </span><code><span>content</span></code><span>.</span></p><p><span>Using a custom chat template that accepts both string and list-form assistant content, both representations produce </span><strong><span>identical token IDs</span></strong><span>. Model generation succeeds, but </span><code><span>return_full_text=True</span></code><span> raises:</span></p><pre><code><span>AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'items'</span></code></pre><h3><span>Reproduction</span></h3><p><span>Run with Transformers </span><code><span>5.23.0.dev0</span></code><span>, PyTorch, and a CUDA GPU:</span></p><pre><code><span>import torch
from PIL import Image
from transformers import AutoProcessor, pipeline

MODEL = "HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM-256M-Instruct"

template = """
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message['role'] == 'user' -%}
&lt;|im_start|&gt;User:
{%- elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
Assistant:
{%- else -%}
{{ message['role'] }}:
{%- endif -%}
{%- if message['content'] is string -%}
{{ message['content'] }}
{%- else -%}
{%- for item in message['content'] -%}
{%- if item['type'] == 'image' -%}
&lt;image&gt;
{%- elif item['type'] == 'text' -%}
{{ item['text'] }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
&lt;end_of_utterance&gt;
{% endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
Assistant:
{%- endif -%}
"""

Image.new("RGB", (224, 224), (230, 20, 20)).save("red.png")

user = {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
        {"type": "image", "path": "red.png"},
        {"type": "text", "text": "What color is this image?"},
    ],
}

list_prefill = [
    user,
    {"role": "assistant", "content": [
        {"type": "text", "text": "The color is"}
    ]},
]

string_prefill = [
    user,
    {"role": "assistant", "content": "The color is"},
]

processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(MODEL)

def encode(chat):
    return processor.apply_chat_template(
        chat,
        chat_template=template,
        continue_final_message=True,
        tokenize=True,
        return_dict=True,
        return_tensors="pt",
    )["input_ids"]

assert torch.equal(encode(list_prefill), encode(string_prefill))

pipe = pipeline(
    "image-text-to-text",
    model=MODEL,
    device=0,
    dtype=torch.float16,
)

def generate(chat, full):
    return pipe(
        text=chat,
        chat_template=template,
        continue_final_message=True,
        return_full_text=full,
        generate_kwargs={"max_new_tokens": 3, "do_sample": False},
    )

print(generate(list_prefill, True))       # PASS
print(generate(string_prefill, False))   # PASS
print(generate(string_prefill, True))    # FAIL</span></code></pre><h3><span>Actual results</span></h3>
Configuration | Result
-- | --
List-form prefill + full text | PASS: The color is red.
String-form prefill + new text | PASS:  red.
String-form prefill + full text | FAIL: AttributeError
List/string prefill token IDs | Exact parity

<p><strong><span>Root cause</span></strong></p><p><span>Both </span><code><span>ImageTextToTextPipeline.postprocess()</span></code><span> and </span><code><span>AnyToAnyPipeline.postprocess()</span></code><span> assume the final assistant content is a list of dictionaries:</span></p><pre><code><span>new_text = dict(prompt_text.messages[-1]["content"][-1].items())
new_text["text"] += generated_text</span></code></pre><p><span>When </span><code><span>content</span></code><span> is a string, indexing returns a character instead of a dictionary, causing </span><code><span>.items()</span></code><span> to fail.</span></p><p><span>The same source-level failure was reproduced in both multimodal pipelines.</span></p><p><strong><span>Scope:</span></strong><span> The default SmolVLM template rejects this particular string prefill. The reproducer uses a custom template that accepts both formats and produces identical token IDs. Public pipeline batching was separately tested and works correctly.</span></p><p><span></span></p><!--EndFragment-->
</body>
</html>

### Expected behavior

When the configured chat template accepts string-valued assistant prefill, `return_full_text=True` should successfully append generated text while preserving the original content representation.

Expected result:

```python
{"role": "assistant", "content": "The color is red."}
```

Both string-form and list-form assistant prefill should produce correct reconstructed responses without postprocessing errors. Existing behavior for list-form multimodal content must remain unchanged.

